{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And he stood between the dead, etc.</b> It may be explained according to the words of our Sages of blessed memory (Tanchuma, Tetzaveh 15), who said that he seized the destroying angel and held him back from destroying, and he counted the dead so that he would add no more upon them. And this is the verse's saying <b>and he stood between the dead and between the living</b> — meaning that he set a boundary to the number of the dead from among the living, so that the plague would not continue. And therefore it says <b>and the dead in the plague were fourteen thousand and seven hundred</b>, to say: these are they who were counted as the number of the dead; <b>and the plague was halted</b> — that it would not continue to strike beyond this number."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:10:38.558731035Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}